Quiniela · discarded ideas
==============================================================================
Read before every brainstorming: everything here has already been discussed and
discarded. Each idea has its date and its reason. If things change (a new source
appears, the cost drops), it can be taken up again: move it to TODO.todo with the
reason.
Format: ✗ discarded · ~ parked (only if a condition is met)


Models
==============================================================================
  ✗ Club strength (ClubElo) as an input of a v5 (v3 + Elo). Discarded on 2026-11-27:
    - The API (api.clubelo.com, the one soccerdata uses) is retired: it does not
      answer and the /API page of the new website redirects to the home page. The
      page of each club only has the Elo since December 2022 (it does not cover the
      backtest from 2015-16).
    - An Elo of our own with our data (leagues only, no cups or Europe) would be
      almost a duplicate of v4 (pi-ratings, learned from the same results), and v3
      shows that those models add nothing on top of the market.
    - Cheap tests if the idea comes back, with no new source: the v4 pi-rating
      difference as an input of v3, and a proxy for "plays in Europe" (previous
      season's table and the fixed UEFA calendar).
    - Replacement under study (TODO.todo): a global rating of our own, with the
      European leagues of football-data and the European cups of ESPN.

  ✗ Dynamic Bayesian models (full MCMC: footBayes, Stan, PyMC; Macrì-Demartino,
    Egidi and Torelli, JRSS-C 2026; and their fast score-driven / GAS version,
    Koopman and Lit). Discarded on 2026-11-27: not worth the computation they need.
    Refitting a full Bayesian model every week of an 11-season backtest would take
    hours or days, and the expected gain on top of the market is a few thousandths
    of log-loss at most; the pi-ratings are already dynamic, so the GAS version
    would add little too.

  ✗ Pinnacle (PS) as a term of its own in v3's pool. Discarded on 2026-11-27:
    football-data stopped publishing Pinnacle's odds in January 2026 (about 100% of
    the matches from 2012-13 to December 2025, 42-50% in January 2026, none since
    February 2026 nor in 2026-27), so the weekly predictions would never have it.
    Betfair Exchange (BFE), the other sharp price, only exists since 2024-25: too
    short for the five years the pool trains on.

  ✗ Spread between bookmakers as an input of v3 (an interaction that lowers the
    weight of the market when bookmakers disagree). Discarded on 2026-11-27 after a
    screening test: v3's pool refitted season by season on the backtest
    probabilities (out-of-sample Dixon-Coles + market), 2016-17 to 2025-26, about
    8,400 matches:
    - mean log(Max / Avg) (BbMx / BbAv before 2019-20): log-loss 1.00451 against
      1.00441 without it (0.0001 worse; better in 4 of 10 seasons);
    - standard deviation between single bookmakers: 1.00550 (0.0011 worse; 2 of 10);
    - its weight comes out close to 0 and changes sign between seasons.
    As a predictability measure it mostly repeats the favourite's probability
    (correlation 0.56) and separates far less than v3's entropy (v3 hit rate from
    70% to 36% by entropy quintile, against 46% to 61% by spread quintile). It may
    still be an informative column of the metrics dataset.

  ✗ Gradient boosting (CatBoost...) with pi-ratings as inputs. Discarded on
    2026-11-27: it finished 16th in the 2023 Soccer Prediction Challenge (Yeung et
    al.), and v3's log-linear pool already combines the models with the market.

  ✗ Men's v4 (pi-ratings) learned from shots on target as a model of its own.
    Discarded on 2026-11-27: v4 does not beat v3, and in La Liga and Segunda the
    odds already reflect the shots. Shots on target are tested in Liga F instead
    (no odds there).


Data sources
==============================================================================
  ✗ Understat xG (La Liga only, since 2014-15). Discarded on 2026-11-27: it does not
    cover Segunda (half of the men's matches) and the odds already reflect xG; very
    little is expected on top of v3.

  ✗ Opta Power Rankings (theanalyst.com). Discarded on 2026-11-27: no official
    download or history (only third-party snapshots since 2023), so it does not
    cover the backtest.

  ✗ Line-ups, injuries and suspensions (Sportmonks, Flashscore...). Discarded on
    2026-11-27: paid or protected against scripts, and the market already prices
    them in.

  ✗ FootyStats. Discarded: paid (checked for Liga F and for La Liga / Segunda).

  ✗ Liga F on FBref, Flashscore, Sofascore: bot protection or scripts forbidden.
    StatsBomb open data: Liga F 2023-24 only. football-data.co.uk and TheSportsDB:
    no Liga F.

  ~ Historical odds of the Champions League, national teams and Liga F (The Odds
    API, paid, since 2020). Parked: no free historical source. Its free plan (500
    requests a month) gives current odds: it could be used in current.html only, if
    it is ever worth it.
